[2026-03-15T23:23:40.015Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BvW1QsicJaf6kyD3mtVfdT","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have all the information needed. Let me provide a comprehensive summary of the GoogleFlights app deployment setup.\n\n## GoogleFlights Deployment Summary\n\nBased on my review of the deployment configuration, here's the exact deployment and database reseeding setup:\n\n### **Main Deployment Command**\nFrom `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/package.json`:\n```bash\nnpm run deploy\n```\n\nThis command runs the deployment script at `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/deploy.ts`\n\n### **What the Deploy Script Does**\nThe deploy.ts script performs these sequential steps:\n\n1. **Database Setup (Neon)**\n   - Creates a Neon PostgreSQL project if first deploy\n   - Initializes the database schema via `initSchema()`\n\n2. **Database Seeding**\n   - On first deploy only, calls `truncateAndSeed()` to seed the database\n   - Seeding is automated as part of the first deployment\n\n3. **Build**\n   - Runs `npx vite build`\n   - Builds the app to the `dist` directory\n\n4. **Netlify Deployment**\n   - Creates a Netlify site if needed (on first deploy)\n   - Deploys using: `npx netlify deploy --prod --dir dist --functions ./netlify/functions`\n\n5. **Deployment Record**\n   - Writes deployment info to `deployment.txt` with URL, site ID, and database credentials\n\n### **To Reseed the Database Only**\nIf you need to reseed without redeploying, you can run:\n```bash\nnpx tsx scripts/seed-db.ts <DATABASE_URL>\n```\n\nThe seed script (`seed-db.ts`) will:\n- Truncate all tables in dependency order\n- Seed ~50 major international airports\n- Seed ~20 airlines\n- Seed ~200 flights (including 1,050+ SFO-JFK flights over March 16-April 15)\n- Create test bookings, recent searches, and tracked routes\n\n### **Key Files**\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/package.json` - Scripts and dependencies\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify.toml` - Netlify build config\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/deploy.ts` - Main deployment orchestrator\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/seed-db.ts` - Database seeding logic\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/schema.ts` - Database schema initialization\n\n### **Environment Variables Required**\n- `NEON_API_KEY` - For Neon database creation\n- `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN` - For Netlify deployment\n- `NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG` - For Netlify site creation\n- `DATABASE_URL` - Postgres connection string (auto-populated after first deploy)"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a27a882105fcd005b (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 44403\ntool_uses: 9\nduration_ms: 12252</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5d16018-2020-41b2-88f2-80c18c9d8446","uuid":"779b28e5-5ace-4422-8001-659902b59545","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Quickly find how the GoogleFlights app is deployed. Look at AGENTS.md, any deploy scripts, netlify.toml, and package.json scripts. I need to know the exact command to redeploy/reseed the database. Check /repo/AGENTS.md, /repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify.toml, /repo/apps/GoogleFlights/package.json, and any deploy-related scripts in /repo/scripts/.","agentId":"a27a882105fcd005b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have all the information needed. Let me provide a comprehensive summary of the GoogleFlights app deployment setup.\n\n## GoogleFlights Deployment Summary\n\nBased on my review of the deployment configuration, here's the exact deployment and database reseeding setup:\n\n### **Main Deployment Command**\nFrom `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/package.json`:\n```bash\nnpm run deploy\n```\n\nThis command runs the deployment script at `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/deploy.ts`\n\n### **What the Deploy Script Does**\nThe deploy.ts script performs these sequential steps:\n\n1. **Database Setup (Neon)**\n   - Creates a Neon PostgreSQL project if first deploy\n   - Initializes the database schema via `initSchema()`\n\n2. **Database Seeding**\n   - On first deploy only, calls `truncateAndSeed()` to seed the database\n   - Seeding is automated as part of the first deployment\n\n3. **Build**\n   - Runs `npx vite build`\n   - Builds the app to the `dist` directory\n\n4. **Netlify Deployment**\n   - Creates a Netlify site if needed (on first deploy)\n   - Deploys using: `npx netlify deploy --prod --dir dist --functions ./netlify/functions`\n\n5. **Deployment Record**\n   - Writes deployment info to `deployment.txt` with URL, site ID, and database credentials\n\n### **To Reseed the Database Only**\nIf you need to reseed without redeploying, you can run:\n```bash\nnpx tsx scripts/seed-db.ts <DATABASE_URL>\n```\n\nThe seed script (`seed-db.ts`) will:\n- Truncate all tables in dependency order\n- Seed ~50 major international airports\n- Seed ~20 airlines\n- Seed ~200 flights (including 1,050+ SFO-JFK flights over March 16-April 15)\n- Create test bookings, recent searches, and tracked routes\n\n### **Key Files**\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/package.json` - Scripts and dependencies\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify.toml` - Netlify build config\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/deploy.ts` - Main deployment orchestrator\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/seed-db.ts` - Database seeding logic\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/scripts/schema.ts` - Database schema initialization\n\n### **Environment Variables Required**\n- `NEON_API_KEY` - For Neon database creation\n- `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN` - For Netlify deployment\n- `NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG` - For Netlify site creation\n- `DATABASE_URL` - Postgres connection string (auto-populated after first deploy)"}],"totalDurationMs":12252,"totalTokens":44403,"totalToolUseCount":9,"usage":{"input_tokens":266,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19731,"cache_read_input_tokens":23745,"output_tokens":661,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"epheme